  "title": "Week 29: Figma Teaching Week 1",
  "date": "2026-07-23T21:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Week 29: Figma Teaching Week 1\n\nThis week, I got a job to teach \"Design System with Figma and AI\". The slides can be checked here.\n\ncover\n\nThe course is separated in three parts.\n\nFoundation of Design Systems\n\nBuilding Design Systems\n\nApplication, Audit and Communication\n\nThe first two parts are taught this week.\n\nFoundation of Design Systems\n\nIntroduction\n\nThe first day, we talked about:\n\nThe history of design systems\n\nPrototyping tools\n\nUsage of Figma Chrome Extension\n\nUse Lovable, v0, Bolt.new and figma make to make designs\n\nDesigns for different platforms, including web, mobile, watches, car, TV and XR.\n\nThe learnings:\n\nFigJam\n\nFigma Chrome Extension\n\nThe first day of work is to make one plan of your personal design. Make a structure of one page(wireframe, with current design systems or using AI), describe what you want to make.\n\nBe Careful\nSome students may focus too much on the AI. Should let them do one design is fine. And make sure the pasted structure is not a screenshot, it should be editable.\n\nDesign Tokens\n\nThe second day, Design Tokens, majorly focusing on:\n\nFigma styles and variables.\n\nThe importance of semantic naming.\n\nHow design tokens were gradually formed.\n\nHow to create Design Tokens in Figma.\n\nHow to use Design Tokens in Figma.\n\nHow to make color palette\n\nHow to use AI to generate size/space tokens\n\nThe learnings:\n\nFigma Styles\n\nFigma Variables\n\nMaterial Theme Builder\n\nColor Wheel\n\nThe second day is to apply the design tokens on the structure page built in the first day.\n\nBe Careful\nThe AI can not generate a token file correctly, need a example JSON file. And students will try to use AI generated color palette, which can be hardly used.\n\nBuilding Design Systems\n\nAtomic Design\n\nThe third day, we talked about atomic design.\n\nModern Workflow from design to dev and publishing\n\nVersion control\n\nUse figma to build atoms\n\nAtoms in the design systems\n\nHow to use the atoms in the current design systems\n\nThe learnings:\n\nZeplin\n\nFigma Component\n\nFigma Variants\n\nThe third day, students should list the atoms that will be used in their page. And build one component set of one component.\n\nBe Careful\nThe students should push their work on zeplin before working and after, to see the difference between v1 and v2. So the students can understand the importance of version control.\n\nAtomic Design with Layouts\n\nThe fourth day, before we head to more complex components. We need to learn layouts.\n\nThe learnings:\n\nFigma Rulers\n\nText Alignments\n\nAuto Layout\n\nThen we start to make more complex components.\n\nThe learnings:\n\nInstance swap\n\nSlots\n\nThis day, students need to make a complex component, like a card or a dialog.\n\nTeam Up\n\nThe fifth day, students should finish their first page, and make their future plans, list the design tokens and the atoms.\n\nI am quite satisfied with the results. Eventually we got four finished projects:\n\nAn XR Music player, with tuned Horizon OS UI\n\nA job seeking website, with his own design system\n\nA mobile food delivery APP, with Apple iOS UI and his own design system\n\nA mobile weekly journal APP, with AI generated(figma make) design system\n\nThe voting logic is that each one have three tickets (1, 2, 3), they can put the score into the top 3 ideal projects (own project excluded). The highest two scored projects will be developed next week.\n\nFinally, the Weekly Journal APP and the XR Music player will be developed next week.\n\nBe careful\nMake sure they make the real components with variants in design. May be allow them to pitch with their own device instead of using the jam board.\n\njam board",
